//! * OAuth token responses need not carry an audience, so "check the audience of
//!   the response" is not a check that exists to be written.
//!
//! # What this platform can do
//!
//! SHA-256, HMAC-SHA256, and secp256k1 Schnorr. **No RSA, no P-256.** So there
//! are exactly two regimes, and local JWT signature verification is not one of
//! them:
//!
//! | Regime | Authenticated by | Egress |
//! | --- | --- | --- |
//! | **Self-issued** (default) | The app IS the authorization server. Every claim is inside an HMAC under the relay identity. | none |
//! | **Delegated** | RFC 7662 introspection. The **AS's answer** is the authority; the token body is never read. | the AS introspection host |
//!
