/// Verify a self-issued token and return its claims.
///
/// The order is the whole point: **the MAC is checked before any claim is read.**
/// Reading a claim first — even to decide which key to use — would be acting on
/// attacker-controlled data.
///
/// Then, in order: the issuer is the one expected, the audience is this server
/// rather than merely present, and the expiry is in the future against
/// message-carried `now_ms`. Scope is the caller's to check separately, because
/// the required set depends on the operation.
